      <title>Andreas Almgren wins NYC Marathon debut in 2:06:01; Chepkirui regains women's title</title>
      <link>https://worldathletics.org/news/report/new-york-city-marathon-2026-almgren-chepkirui</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://worldathletics.org/news/report/new-york-city-marathon-2026-almgren-chepkirui</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 01 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700</pubDate>
      <category>Running</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://assets.aws.worldathletics.org/large/6ae77cd53353f6727d15e498.jpg" alt="Andreas Almgren at the 2026 NYC Marathon, via World Athletics" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>The Swede ran 2:06:01, breaking away from Yeman Crippa late. He picked New York because position matters more than the clock there. Chepkirui regained the women's title.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;I didn't really look at my watch or the time or try to calculate a finishing time or anything. I just tried to stay up in the front then see what happened.&rdquo; - <a href="https://run247.com/running-news/marathon-news/andreas-almgren-new-york-city-marathon-2026-reaction">Andreas Almgren, at the post-race press conference</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;It would have been nice to have a 2:05 time, but I'm very happy about the win.&rdquo; - <a href="https://run247.com/running-news/marathon-news/andreas-almgren-new-york-city-marathon-2026-reaction">Almgren</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://worldathletics.org/news/report/new-york-city-marathon-2026-almgren-chepkirui">World Athletics</a> &middot; <a href="https://run247.com/running-news/marathon-news/andreas-almgren-new-york-city-marathon-2026-reaction">RUN247</a> &middot; <a href="https://www.runningusa.org/industry-news/2026-tcs-new-york-city-marathon-becomes-the-first-marathon-ever-to-exceed-60000-finisher-mark/">Running USA (60,000 finishers)</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20loved%20%22Andreas%20Almgren%20wins%20NYC%20Marathon%20debut...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Andreas%20Almgren%20wins%20NYC%20Marathon%20debut...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20less%20like%20%22Andreas%20Almgren%20wins%20NYC%20Marathon%20debut...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//worldathletics.org/news/report/new-york-city-marathon-2026-almgren-chepkirui%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
