    <item>
      <title>SF voters pass Props D, E and F after $14M billionaire-backed campaign, handing Lurie sole power over department heads</title>
      <link>https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://missionlocal.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/9R0A3649-2-scaled.jpeg" alt="Daniel Lurie at his election watch party, photo by Genesia Ting for Mission Local" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>Props D, E and F passed with roughly $14M in billionaire backing, handing the mayor more control over ballots, contracts and department heads. Analysts say the blame game ends here.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;These charter reform measures will make it very hard now for mayors to argue credibly that they don't have the authority to do what voters ask of them.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Jason McDaniel, SFSU political science professor</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;He has all the power he asked for. Let's see what he does with it.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Eric Jaye, Democratic political consultant</a></blockquote>
<blockquote>&ldquo;These victories are not a finish line, they are a starting point.&rdquo; - <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Daniel Lurie, in his victory speech Tuesday night</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/">Mission Local</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20loved%20%22SF%20voters%20pass%20Props%20D%2C%20E%20and%20F%20after%20%24...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20meh%20on%20%22SF%20voters%20pass%20Props%20D%2C%20E%20and%20F%20after%20%24...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20less%20like%20%22SF%20voters%20pass%20Props%20D%2C%20E%20and%20F%20after%20%24...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//missionlocal.org/2026/11/daniel-lurie-election-city-hall-power/%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
      <media:content url="https://missionlocal.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/9R0A3649-2-scaled.jpeg" medium="image"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Regional Transit Measure passes with 62% region-wide and 79% in SF; ~$1B/yr sales tax saves BART, Muni, Caltrain from 2027 cuts</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/san-francisco-bay-area-transit-bart-muni</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/san-francisco-bay-area-transit-bart-muni</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 07:00:00 -0800</pubDate>
      <category>San Francisco</category>
      <description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/c3d3692d31216c33cdb6a5bf1402e4dc4b04cdc3/376_0_4319_3456/master/4319.jpg?width=1200&amp;height=630&amp;quality=85&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;precrop=40:21,offset-x50,offset-y0&amp;overlay-align=bottom%2Cleft&amp;overlay-width=100p&amp;overlay-base64=L2ltZy9zdGF0aWMvb3ZlcmxheXMvdGctZGVmYXVsdC5wbmc&amp;enable=upscale&amp;s=1857f547ba082ab55c00f36db8f33d6f" alt="Bay Area transit photo via The Guardian" style="max-width:100%"/></p>
<p><b>The Regional Transit Measure, a sales tax worth roughly $1B a year for BART, Muni, Caltrain and AC Transit, won 62% region-wide and 79% in SF. Prop H's Muni parcel tax took 74%.</b></p>
<blockquote>&ldquo;This is existential, especially for BART.&rdquo; - <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/03/bay-area-transit-tax-bart-caltrain/">Tom Radulovich, former BART board member, before the vote</a></blockquote>
<p>Sources: <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/san-francisco-bay-area-transit-bart-muni">The Guardian</a> &middot; <a href="https://sfstandard.com/2026/11/03/bay-area-transit-tax-bart-caltrain/">SF Standard</a> &middot; <a href="https://mtc.ca.gov/news/bay-area-voters-show-strong-support-public-transit">MTC</a></p>
<p>Feedback: <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20loved%20%22Regional%20Transit%20Measure%20passes%20with%2062...%22">Loved it</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20meh%20on%20%22Regional%20Transit%20Measure%20passes%20with%2062...%22">Meh</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=Digest%2011/7%3A%20less%20like%20%22Regional%20Transit%20Measure%20passes%20with%2062...%22">Less of this</a> &middot; <a href="sms:+16506139572?&amp;body=https%3A//www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/07/san-francisco-bay-area-transit-bart-muni%0A">Chat about it</a></p>]]></description>
